  "doc_revision": "TK Series Simultaneous Heating&Cooling Output PID Temperature Controllers, Communication Manual MCT-TKC1-V2.2-EN",
  "verified": false,
  "notes": "The manual is a series-level manual ('TK Series'); the register chapter does not name TK4S, so model-specific features (heater current, DI-2, AL3, cooling MV) may be absent on a given TK4S variant. The manual lists each item as 'No(Address)', e.g. 400001(0000), 301001(03E8): the 0xxxxx/1xxxxx/3xxxxx/4xxxxx numbers are 1-based reference numbers and the hex value in parentheses is the 0-based protocol address. This preset uses the parenthesised protocol addresses with address_base=0: coils (FC01/05), discrete inputs (FC02), input registers (FC04: PV etc. at 0x03E8..0x03EF) and holding registers (FC03/06/16: groups 0x0000.., 0x0032.., comm group 0x00DA..). Values are integers with the decimal point defined by the 'Decimal Point' input register (0:0, 1:0.0, 2:0.00, 3:0.000); they are exposed raw (scale 1) because the scale is dynamic. H-MV/C-MV 0..1000 = 0.0..100.0 % (scale 0.1). Data signedness is not stated explicitly; int16 chosen for PV/SV/alarm values because the ranges include negative numbers (-1999, -30000). Defaults from the Default column: address 1, 9600 bps (2:96), parity NONE, stop bits 2 ('1: 2'), response wait 20 ms; data bits not stated in the portion read. Unit indicators (discrete inputs 0x0000/0x0001) and reserved/model-name/version registers are omitted. Whether comm parameter changes need a restart is not stated. Some parameter-group items may only be writable in certain modes (e.g. H-MV only in MAN) - not stated.",
